# Files served read-only at /AOK/bundled, embedded into the kernel by
# tools/gen-aokfs.py at build time (see meson.build's aok_libs_groups).
#
# Programs and libraries built AHEAD OF TIME for guest roots, so that a setup
# script links them in rather than compiling on the device -- wf-panel's
# build ran an A10X iPad out of memory, and the shims want a compiler most
# roots do not have. tools/build-bundled.sh builds them on a Mac, in the CLI's
# guest roots, with the same scripts a device would run; the results are
# committed under opt/AOK/bundled/.
#
# One directory per target: a distro release and architecture for what links
# against a distro's own libraries (devuan6-aarch64: wf-panel, good only for
# the wf-shell version in wf-panel.source; arm64 only, the fastest guest), a libc and architecture for what
# links only against libc (glibc-x86_64: the shims).
#
# Each line: <path> [mode]   read from opt/AOK/bundled/<path>.
devuan6-aarch64/wf-panel 0555
devuan6-aarch64/wf-panel.source
glibc-aarch64/libish-wl-release-guard.so 0555
glibc-aarch64/libish-pixman.so 0555
glibc-x86_64/libish-wl-release-guard.so 0555
glibc-x86_64/libish-pixman.so 0555
musl-aarch64/libish-wl-release-guard.so 0555
musl-aarch64/libish-pixman.so 0555
musl-x86_64/libish-wl-release-guard.so 0555
musl-x86_64/libish-pixman.so 0555
